<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chincha Islands War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1864">1864</a>–<a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chincha-islands">Chincha Islands</a> War was a conflict between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and its former colonies <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> and Chile, later joined by Ecuador and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a>, from 1864 to 1866. It began when a Spanish squadron seized Peru's guano-rich Chincha Islands. In 1866 the Spanish bombarded the undefended port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valparaiso">Valparaíso</a> and then attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/callao">Callao</a> before withdrawing; a final peace was signed only in the 1870s and 1880s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chincha-islands-war.jpg" alt="Chincha Islands War" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CombateDosdeMayo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
